;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ROBINSPR.MAC -- sprite frame data.
;
; Ported from the ZX original, $8E24-$AA30.  Labels keep the original
; addresses: L<hex address>.
;
; Frames are reached through the pointer table at $8D80 (73. words), which
; $C6D6 indexes by doubling an animation frame number.  Robin's object record
; uses $8D80 as its base; other actors point $C6D8 at $8DC4 or $8DEA first, so
; the same table serves everyone at three different origins.  Bit 7 of a frame
; number selects the mirrored variant, produced at draw time by $C8B7 through
; the bit-reversal table rather than stored here.
;
; Each frame starts with a 3-byte header consumed by $C585/$C790 -- the first
; byte carries the width class compared against 4 and, in bit 7, a flag that
; patches the glyph draw loop -- followed by the frame's glyph rows, which
; $C6D6 XORs into the shadow bitmap.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------

